You need to select functionality that meets the requirement.  

Which features should you use? Each feature may be used once or not at all.

<DragDrop
  items={["Posting layer - custom","Posting layer - current","Posting layer - tax"]}
  slots={[{"answer":"Posting layer - custom","id":"pickling_machine_depreciation","label":"Pickling machine depreciation"},{"answer":"Posting layer - current","id":"regular_depreciation","label":"Regular depreciation"}]}
  explanation={"A custom posting layer keeps depreciation for a specific asset or specialized accounting purpose separate from standard book postings. Regular depreciation uses the current posting layer; the tax layer is reserved for tax depreciation."}
/>","className":"button hollow icon-accent icon-only question-actions"}],A company uses Dynamics 365 Finance for its accounts payable processing.  

A vendor offers a special installment term that lets the company invoice with three equal installment payments. The first payment is due 60 days after the invoice date. The second payment is due 90 days after the invoice date. The final payment is due 120 days after the invoice date. The company pays each invoice on its due date to take advantage of these terms.  

You need to configure the terms of payment and payment schedule for the vendor master record.  

How should you configure and assign the vendor master record?

You need to configure revenue recognition.  

Which revenue type is associated with each line of business? Each revenue type may be used once, more than once, or not at all.  



<DragDrop
  items={["Essential","Non-essential","Post contract support (PCS)"]}
  slots={[{"answer":"Essential","id":"web_design","label":"Web design"},{"answer":"Non-essential","id":"video_platform","label":"Video platform"}]}
  reuse={true}
  explanation={"An Essential revenue type is a main source of an organization’s revenue, while a Non-essential type is not. Web design represents 60 percent of revenue and is essential; the video platform represents 5 percent and is non-essential. PCS is for an item that supports other sold items, which does not apply to either line.\
\
**Learn more:** [Revenue recognition setup - Finance | Dynamics 365](https://learn.microsoft.com/es-es/dynamics365/finance/accounts-receivable/revenue-recognition-setup)"}
